Jack Bolsen <jbolsen@verizon.net> wrote:
>real wizard. Similar problems exist with ettins and minotaurs (both are 
>a light brown H) as well as monsters that are identified with a q.

There are only four functionally distinct kinds of 'q', despite the
large number of species of 'q'.  There are those that hit hard (light
grey - mumakil, baluchitheria, and titanotheres; dark grey/dark blue -
mastodons), those that move fast (red - leocrottas), those that move
incredibly slowly and ignore pits (cyan - wumpuses), and those that are
generated in packs (brown - rothes).

All the *important* differences are visible on a colour terminal.  If
your character cares about the difference between a mumak and a
baluchitherium, he probably can't really afford to fight either of them.

