They cannot support the Windows version. (Well, strictly speaking, they
could, but they'd have to rip the entire display subsystem to pieces in
order to do it, *and* write a separate client interface program that
ran on your PC, and they'd *still* need to provide support for the
tty version.)

They may be able to support one of the X11-based windowing options, if
it does not excessively increase the load on their servers.  Try asking
them nicely by private e-mail.
